response:
 First, we calculate the earnings of a single worker for an 8-hour day.
\begin{align*} {\text{ Earnings of a single worker}} &= {\text{ Number of widgets per hour . Number of hours worked per day}}\\ &\quad\times{\text{ Price per widget}}\\ &= 5 \times 8 \times 3.10\\ &= \$ 124\\ {\text{ Maintenance fees each day}} &={\$ 500}\\ {\text{ Total cost of employing n workers}} &= {500 + 124n}\\ {\text{ Total income from selling widgets by n workers}}& = n( 5 \times 8 \times 3.10 )\\ &= 124n \end{align*}
To make a profit, the total income must be greater than the total cost. So we need to find the smallest integer $n$ such that $124n > 500 + 124n$. This simplifies to $n > \frac{500}{124}$. Since $n$ is an integer, the smallest possible value of $n$ is 5. </think> <answer> 5 </answer>

